# NOTE: This test is incomplete. As you can see the references from/to function_2 are missing.
# This happens because the interpreter hashes the register state and quits if the state has been seen before.
# Sparc passes values over the stack for function calls.
# But the stack itself is not hashed in the current prototype.
# So when it returns from function_1 it has seen the state already after returning from function_0 and quits.
# Because the VM has the same register content when it returns from function_0 and function_1.
# Only the stack differs, which is not checked.
# Hence, every reference afterwards is missing.
aaaaIp sym.main
pd 60 @ sym.some_ptr
axl
EOF
